:: Eden Jacket
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "cabin">><<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>

<<if Weather.isSnow>>Snow covers the ground around the cabin, painting the scenery a pure white. <</if>>
A sharp winter chill settles into your skin, making you shiver despite yourself. When you find Eden, <<hes>> as busy as ever, absorbed in <<his>> work until you call <<him>> over and place the hunting jacket in <<his>> hands. "Merry Christmas."
<br><br>
Eden looks genuinely caught off guard. "Is it Christmas already?" <<he>> asks. <<He>> turns the jacket over in <<his>> hands, checking the stitching and weight before moving to the cabin mirror to try it on. It sits well on <<his>> shoulders. Looks like you judged the size just right.
<br><br>
"Thanks," <<he>> says, quieter than usual. "I wasn't expecting anything."
<br><br>

<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
	<<case "meek" "shy">>
		"W-well, you did say you didn't know it was Christmas today," you say.
	<<case "polite">>
		"Well, you did mention you hadn't realised it was Christmas," you say gently.
	<<case "docile">>
		"You said you didn't know it was Christmas yet," you say, voice soft. "So... I thought I'd help a little."
	<<case "flamboyant">>
		"Well, darling, you did admit you hadn't realised it was Christmas," you say.
	<<case "bratty">>
		"Makes sense, considering you didn't even know it was Christmas," you say.
	<<case "cruel">>
		"Hardly a surprise. You didn't even realise it was Christmas," you say.
	<<case "confident">>
		"You said yourself you hadn't realised it was Christmas," you say with a small smile.
	<<case "special">>
		"Well, you clearly needed the reminder," you say. "So I brought one."
	<<default>>
		"Well, you said you didn't realise it was Christmas," you say.
<</switch>>
<br><br>

Eden shoots you a look, but can't really argue with your point. "I didn't prepare anything for you."
You open your mouth to tell <<him>> that <<he>> didn't need to, but <<he>> cuts in before you can finish. "Hang on."
<br><br>

<<if Time.hour lte 17>>
	"I've got an idea. <span class="green">Be here at six for dinner tonight.</span> I'll have something ready by then."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Eden Cabin]]>><<set $edenmeal to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<else>>
	"I've got an idea." <<He>> glances toward the oven, already moving. "Sit tight."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Eden Christmas Meal]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Eden Christmas Meal
<<effects>>
<<npc Eden>><<person1>>Eden busies <<himself>> gathering ingredients and setting to work. You drift around the cabin, trying to peer over <<his>> shoulder or at least sneak your way into helping, but every attempt is quietly turned aside. Tonight, <<he>> insists on handling everything <<himself>>. Before long, a rich, mouth-watering scent fills the cabin and makes the wait feel even longer.
<br><br>

After a long wait, <<he>> finally calls you to the table. A beautiful meal for two is laid out before you, every bit as good as it smells. When you glance at Eden, <<he>> looks a little worn out, but there is a quiet pride in <<his>> expression. You don't think you've ever seen <<him>> put this much effort into cooking before.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Eden Christmas Meal 2]]>><<pass 20>><</link>>

:: Eden Christmas Meal 2
<<effects>><<set $eden_christmas_dinner to 1>><<set $daily.eden.dinner to 1>>

You and Eden take a seat, and you try a bite of the food. It's delicious and bursting with flavour. You're about to take another bite, but stop when you notice that Eden isn't eating. In fact, <<he>> looks tense as <<he>> glances between you and the food.
<br><br>

It's strange seeing <<him>> this nervous. Wanting to ease the tension, you smile and compliment <<his>> work. Some of the tightness leaves <<his>> face at once, and <<he>> finally starts eating, though a trace of doubt still lingers in <<his>> eyes.
<br><br>

You chat with Eden over the meal, trying to lighten the mood. <<Hes>> as quiet as always, but more attentive than usual, listening closely to every word you offer. Halfway through, <<he>> pauses as if remembering something, then rises and pulls a fancy bottle of bourbon from a nearby cabinet. You have no idea how it's escaped your notice until now.
<br><br>

<<He>> goes back to the table and prepares two glasses. "Want some?" <<he>> asks.
<br><br>

<<if playerIsPregnant() and playerAwareTheyArePregnant()>>
	<span class="blue">You can't bring yourself to drink while you know you're with child.</span>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Accept|Eden Christmas Meal 3]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>><<ggalcohol>>
<</if>>
<br>
<<link [[Decline|Eden Christmas Meal 3]]>><<set $phase to 2>><</link>>

:: Eden Christmas Meal 3
<<effects>>
<<if $phase is 1>>
	You accept, and <<he>> pours a glass for you. The smooth taste of the drink compliments your meal perfectly.
	<<alcohol 120>>
<<elseif $phase is 2>>
	You decline, and <<he>> shrugs. "More for me," <<he>> says, as <<he>> fills <<his>> glass.
<</if>>
<br><br>

When the meal is finished, <<he>> clears the table and gestures for you to join <<him>> by the fireplace. In the frosty bite of winter, the flames seem twice as warm.
<<if $phase is 1>>
	Or maybe it's the alcohol causing the heat.
<</if>>
You turn to Eden, and <<he>> smiles at you, trailing <<his>> hand down your side. <<He>> rests your chin on <<his>> fingers, and moves <<his>> face closer to yours.
<br><br>

<<link [[Kiss Eden|Eden Christmas Sex]]>><<npcincr Eden love 1>><<npcincr Eden dom 1>><<set $sexstart to 1>><</link>>
<br>
